    "lawCode": "Amd §§4 & 5, Chap 199 of 2008",
    "lawSection": "Housing",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8073\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend chapter 199 of the laws of 2008 amending the private housing\nfinance law relating to the low income housing trust fund program, in\nrelation to reporting by the housing trust fund corporation and the\neffectiveness of such provisions\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend\na program administered by the Housing Trust Fund Corporation to\nrehabilitate housing in distressed communities.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nThis bill would extend a program\nadministered by the Housing Trust Fund corporation to rehabilitate\nhousing in distressed communities until July 1, 2011. It would also\nrequire a report on the units assisted under the Low Income\nHousing Trust Fund to the chairs of the Assembly Housing Committee\nand the Senate Housing, Construction and Community Development on an\nannual basis.\n\nEFFECTS OF PRESENT LAW WHICH THIS BILL WOULD ALTER:\nThis bill would\namend sections 4 and 5 of chapter 199 of the laws of 2008 amending\nthe private housing finance law.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe Housing Trust Fund Corporation has provided housing\nto distressed communities in the State of New York for many years.\nThis legislation would ensure that this corporation continues to be of\nassistance to those who are in need of housing. It also requires that\nthe corporation provide a report to the Legislature on an annual\nbasis on the units assisted by the Low Income Housing Trust Fund, to\nshow the progress of housing affordability in New York.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nThis is new legislation.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided,\nhowever, that, sections one, two and four of this act shall expire\nand be deemed repealed July 1, 2011; provided further, however that\nany awards made prior to such repeal date shall remain in effect on\nand after such date.\n\n",
